                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bought this ages ago, played it recently (thankfully after quality of life patch, lucky there I suppose), took a break and now finished it. This is one of those games where \"Yes or No\" feels kinda like \"Eeeh, could I have middle option?\" where I'm like \"I think there are some things to like if you like dating sims\", but there is lot to improve. Like... I'm mostly choosing recommend on basis of \"I DID finish it\" even if I haven't at time of writing bothered to finish all achievements and since I do feel like I liked it more than disliked it even if its not easy recommend.\n\nSo like, I was expecting scifi military adventure story with romance and maybe some mystery, one of girls was clearly evangelion inspired and aliens on steam store pictures looked bizarre. I guess I was expecting something like Planet Stronghold I suppose? What it IS, is a military themed dating sim(unusual combination of genres, as in I wonder if military fiction and \"go on date with cute girls\" fandoms overlap a lot) where you grind money from fighting aliens for gifts for whole game until its final boss time. There are small hints of \"some kind of conspiracy is going and there is something suspicious about the strange geometric aliens\"(speaking of which, some of organic ones look bit more placeholdery than others) but as it turns out none of that is explored at all until an exposition dump in Eve's ending. Basically yeaaah, don't expect plot in this game. I do appreacite there being rpg combat minigame, but its really tedious one overall(good thing quality of life patches added speeding up feature), doesn't help that most powerful abilities cost money, which is same resource you need to get stronger and to buy gifts for dating sim aspect. I did get really lucky with lucky pendants(rare drop worth tons of money but also which instantly brings character to next relationship status if you gift it) on my playthrough though so that made things smoother.\n\nYou can already see what the art is like from steam store and form opinion on that.(its not bad, but doesn't standout among anime style games either) Voice acting wise its bit of hit and miss, like most of performances are good or good enough, then there is one that sounds like reading lines from script without emoting much even when clearly the situation is calling to sound sad or yell commands or such.\n\nSo yeah there are some fun moments to enjoy, but overall its mostly gameplay wise tedious grinding (fight with enemies feels sometimes like it takes too long and ALL of them having access to shield that lasts multiple turns doesn't help). Basically if you have extreme patience to finish game, then yeah sure go for it if its your jam. Its not what I expected or wanted, but I did enjoy things like Cecile & Jen's vitriolic dynamic and I wouldn't mind to see improved second attempt.",
